# Live database access

## Allowed

- **Read-only** queries against live Supabase/Postgres (`SELECT` / `.select()` / inspect rows) when needed to debug or answer questions

## Never do yourself

- `INSERT` / `UPDATE` / `DELETE` / upserts / backfills / running destructive migration SQL against live data
- Any service-role script that mutates rows

## When the user asks to change or delete data

Give them SQL to run — **SELECT first**, then the destructive statement:

```sql
-- 1) Inspect
select id, buyer_email, status
from public.orders
where id = 400;

-- 2) Destructive (user runs only if select looks right)
delete from public.order_products where order_id = 400;
delete from public.orders where id = 400;
```

Do not execute step 2 yourself, even if they say "delete it" — hand them the queries unless they explicitly say you may run the write (default: **never write**).
